M10 attack scripts: save the node/target id tables set in Created().

M10_Stealth_Attack_01/02 fill attack_loc[13] and M10_Mammoth_Attack fills
target[4] with level object ids in Created(), and _02 clears same there.
Created() does not run when a save is loaded, and these members were not
registered, so after a load the tables hold zeros (script factory
value-initialisation): every Find_Object returns NULL and the stealth tanks
path toward the world origin instead of the attack nodes. Register them under
unused SAVE_VARIABLE ids (_01 attack_loc 9; _02 attack_loc 8, same 9;
Mammoth target 4). Saves made before this patch load the tables as zero, as
before. M10_Mammoth_Attack is not bound in retail M10 data; it is registered
for consistency.

--- a/Mission10.cpp
+++ b/Mission10.cpp
@@ -2414,6 +2414,8 @@
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( attacking, 1 );
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( valid, 2 );
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( choice, 3 );
+		// Vita save/load: the target ids are set only in Created(), which a load skips.
+		SAVE_VARIABLE( target, 4 );
 	}
 
 	void Created(GameObject * obj)
@@ -3074,6 +3076,8 @@
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( loc_dist, 6 );
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( loc, 7 );
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( same, 8 );
+		// Vita save/load: the node ids are set only in Created(), which a load skips.
+		SAVE_VARIABLE( attack_loc, 9 );
 	}
 
 	void Created(GameObject * obj)
@@ -3205,6 +3209,10 @@
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( enemy_loc, 5 );
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( loc_dist, 6 );
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( loc, 7 );
+		// Vita save/load: the node ids and same are set only in Created(), which a
+		// load skips.
+		SAVE_VARIABLE( attack_loc, 8 );
+		SAVE_VARIABLE( same, 9 );
 	}
 
 	void Created(GameObject * obj)
